---
/* L52 - the reliability curve, one point per drawer. One writer: the figures workstream C. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L52.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a filing cabinet with several open drawers full of folders standing on a table, beside a framed grid holding scattered dots and a diagonal line."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L52-fig-title L52-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L52-fig-title">A reliability curve with one point per confidence drawer</title>
      <desc id="L52-fig-desc">
        A square plot with confidence along the bottom and accuracy up the side, and a dashed diagonal running from the bottom left to the top right, labelled calibrated. Five plotted points appear one after another: two sit on the top edge, two on the bottom edge, and one prussian point low and to the right is ringed and labelled promised 0.85, delivered 0. The dashed diagonal draws itself first, then the points fade in.
      </desc>
      <line x1="120" y1="270" x2="570" y2="270" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="120" y1="270" x2="120" y2="50" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 620; --m-duration: 1.2s;" d="M 120 270 L 560 50" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
      <text x="300" y="150" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">calibrated</text>

      <circle class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" cx="538" cy="50" r="5" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.5s;" x="500" y="38" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.95 - 1.0</text>

      <circle class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.75s;" cx="494" cy="270" r="5" fill="var(--color-prussian)" />
      <circle class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.75s;" cx="494" cy="270" r="11" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.75s;" x="512" y="248" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">promised 0.85,</text>
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 0.75s;" x="512" y="264" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">delivered 0</text>

      <circle class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1s;" cx="362" cy="50" r="5" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1s;" x="330" y="38" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.55 - 1.0</text>

      <circle class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.25s;" cx="318" cy="270" r="5" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.25s;" x="268" y="256" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.45 - 0</text>

      <circle class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.5s;" cx="142" cy="50" r="5" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      <text class="m-fade" style="--m-duration: 0.6s; --m-delay: 1.5s;" x="150" y="38" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">0.05 - 1.0</text>

      <text x="300" y="292" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">confidence</text>
      <text x="40" y="170" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">accuracy</text>
      <text x="40" y="312" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">one point per drawer: promise across, outcome up; the average of the gaps is the score</text>

    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L52</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Sorting the results into confidence drawers turns each one into a point - promise across, outcome up - and a point below the diagonal is a promise the model did not keep.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
